We can fix the harvester dragging in and out if the refinery was killed while turning by moving the drag activity from DockingState.Turn to its own case:
```csharp
case DockingState.Drag:
	if (!Refinery.IsInWorld || Refinery.IsDead)
		return true;

	dockingState = DockingState.Dock;
	if (IsDragRequired)
		QueueChild(new Drag(self, StartDrag, EndDrag, DragLength));

	return false;
```

Note that these suggestions don't help with the second glitch in that issue, which is easily reproduced by issuing a move order while the harvester is turning to dock.
